#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235431 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ead734d2-e970-5e92-9ac3-1260bbfab982" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{e}^{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ead734d2-e970-5e92-9ac3-1260bbfab982" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234918} :answer-field/id #uuid "3429cda5-daf9-53dc-9c18-72e4afbade0a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235025}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dabe687a-249f-595c-be70-5214c92992e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-167326" :question/problem "If a curve $C$ is defined by the equation $y=f(x)\\cdot h(x),$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=\\pi .$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        Slope $\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate using the product rule. Recall that $f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}$ and $h(x)=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x})=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =f\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}x}+h\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}\\cdot (-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x} \\\\  & =-2{e}^{x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=\\pi $ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=\\pi } & =-2{e}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ) \\\\  & =-2{e}^{\\pi }(-1+0) \\\\  & =2{e}^{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $2{e}^{\\pi }.$" :step/_content [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235760 :multistep/_steps {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235313 :multistep/context "Consider the following functions: \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x},\\,g(x)=8x-\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3},\\,h(x)=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235608 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235430 :question/math-academy-id "q-167325"}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235626 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235435 :question/math-academy-id "q-167331"}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235646 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235432 :question/math-academy-id "q-167327"}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235726 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235436 :question/math-academy-id "q-167332"}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235739 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235429 :question/math-academy-id "q-167324"}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235760 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235431 :question/math-academy-id "q-167326"}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235765 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235434 :question/math-academy-id "q-167329"}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235781 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235433 :question/math-academy-id "q-167328"}}]}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235477 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bff132e5-2ee2-59aa-8aea-3502c866b4de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4\\operatorname{cos}(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234842}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bff132e5-2ee2-59aa-8aea-3502c866b4de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\operatorname{cos}(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234842} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4cf055c-8ce0-5492-8beb-32c82e4064bc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235248}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6cb1f8a0-05ce-5136-9c47-0498f7e83853" :question/math-academy-id "q-167778" :question/problem "$\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}x}\\,=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We know that \n\n$$\n\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x).\n$$\n\nApplying this formula and the constant multiple rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)) \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :step/_content [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235771 :multistep/_steps {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235296 :multistep/context "Consider the following functions: \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x},\\,g(x)=8x-\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3},\\,h(x)=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\n$$" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235600 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235485 :question/math-academy-id "q-167786"}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235603 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235482 :question/math-academy-id "q-167783"}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235635 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235479 :question/math-academy-id "q-167780"}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235650 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235478 :question/math-academy-id "q-167779"}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235688 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235481 :question/math-academy-id "q-167782"}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235701 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235484 :question/math-academy-id "q-167785"}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235702 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235480 :question/math-academy-id "q-167781"}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235771 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235477 :question/math-academy-id "q-167778"}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235772 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235483 :question/math-academy-id "q-167784"}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235787 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235486 :question/math-academy-id "q-167787"}}]}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235479 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dbf988f2-8940-5547-8a0c-461e7fba4865" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{e}^{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234891}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbf988f2-8940-5547-8a0c-461e7fba4865" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234891} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6fb57fa-80a8-5893-88ed-795c73c49674" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235177}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8af2c303-b3aa-5790-885e-7a978a609bf5" :question/math-academy-id "q-167780" :question/problem "If a curve $C$ is defined by the equation $y=f(x)\\cdot h(x),$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=\\pi .$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        Slope $\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate using the product rule. Recall that $f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}$ and $h(x)=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x})=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =f\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}x}+h\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}\\cdot (-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))+(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x} \\\\  & =-2{e}^{x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=\\pi $ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=\\pi } & =-2{e}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )) \\\\  & =-2{e}^{\\pi }(-1+0) \\\\  & =2{e}^{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $2{e}^{\\pi }.$" :step/_content [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235635 :multistep/_steps {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235296 :multistep/context "Consider the following functions: \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x},\\,g(x)=8x-\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3},\\,h(x)=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\n$$" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235600 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235485 :question/math-academy-id "q-167786"}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235603 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235482 :question/math-academy-id "q-167783"}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235635 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235479 :question/math-academy-id "q-167780"}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235650 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235478 :question/math-academy-id "q-167779"}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235688 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235481 :question/math-academy-id "q-167782"}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235701 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235484 :question/math-academy-id "q-167785"}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235702 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235480 :question/math-academy-id "q-167781"}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235771 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235477 :question/math-academy-id "q-167778"}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235772 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235483 :question/math-academy-id "q-167784"}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235787 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235486 :question/math-academy-id "q-167787"}}]}}]}]}
